# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Function `Lock.extendLock()` is used to reset the lock time and extend the period and token amount to an existing lock. But before extending the period and adding token amount, it did not call `bondNFT.distribute()` first. 

Function `bondNFT.distribute()` is used to calculate, sync the accumulated reward in case new epochs are happened.
```solidity
function distribute(
    address _tigAsset,
    uint _amount
) external {
    if (totalShares[_tigAsset] == 0 || !allowedAsset[_tigAsset]) return;
    IERC20(_tigAsset).transferFrom(_msgSender(), address(this), _amount);
    unchecked {
        uint aEpoch = block.timestamp / DAY;
        if (aEpoch > epoch[_tigAsset]) {
            for (uint i=epoch[_tigAsset]; i<aEpoch; i++) {
                epoch[_tigAsset] += 1;
                accRewardsPerShare[_tigAsset][i+1] = accRewardsPerShare[_tigAsset][i];
            }
        }
        accRewardsPerShare[_tigAsset][aEpoch] += _amount * 1e18 / totalShares[_tigAsset];
    }
    emit Distribution(_tigAsset, _amount);
}
```

It did not call `bondNFT.distribute()` which means current epoch is not synced yet. In addition to that, in function `bondNFT.extendLock()`, it used current epoch value to assign `bondPaid`. The result is `bondPaid[]` used value from previous epoch to calculate, so users can get all reward from last epoch to latest one immediately. 
```solidity
function extendLock(
    uint _id,
    address _asset,
    uint _amount,
    uint _period,
    address _sender
) external onlyManager() {
    ...
    unchecked {
        ...
        bondPaid[_id][bond.asset] = accRewardsPerShare[bond.asset][epoch[bond.asset]] * _bond.shares / 1e18;
    }
    emit ExtendLock(_period, _amount, _sender,  _id);
}
```

