## Impact
According to the Tigris official document, stable vaults and tigUSD can be exchanged 1:1. 

>Tigris's native stablecoins are stablecoins pegged to a currency, backed by a basket of same-type assets. They are redeemable 1:1 for any asset in its respective StableVault, allowing for a very stable peg. The StableVault's purpose is to allow for many tokens of the same kind (such as USDC/DAI/USDT) to be used to trade on Tigris without splitting up the liquidity into multiple individual pools.

Currently, the stable tokens that supported are DAI on the Polygon chain and USDT on the Arbitrum chain. If other stable tokens with different decimals are added or bridges are created, it is possible that an attack using these tokens could occur. The decimals for DAI and USDT are 18 and 6, respectively. This means that an attackers could withdraw more funds than they have deposited.

