# Vulnerability details


In the lock.sol contract the claimGovFees() function poses a reetrancy problem, because if Checks Effects Interactions is not respected in this function the important updates are called after IGovNFT(govNFT).claim(assets[i]); 


    function claimGovFees() public {
        address[] memory assets = bondNFT.getAssets();

        for (uint i=0; i < assets.length; i++) {
            uint balanceBefore = IERC20(assets[i]).balanceOf(address(this));
            IGovNFT(govNFT).claim(assets[i]);
            uint balanceAfter = IERC20(assets[i]).balanceOf(address(this));
            IERC20(assets[i]).approve(address(bondNFT), type(uint256).max);
            bondNFT.distribute(assets[i], balanceAfter - balanceBefore);
        }
    }

Placed at the end of the function claimGovFees() IGovNFT(govNFT).claim after all status updates have occurred. 
And protect the function with a reentrancy-guard.

